WEBVTT

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.240
Naomi Wildman, state
your purpose here.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:11.436
I was waiting for you.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.773
Kadis-Kot, remember?

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.143
Our weekly game?

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.579
Reschedule for tomorrow.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.047
I'm working now.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.675
Redecorating isn't work.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.379
Aesthetics are irrelevant.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.920
I'm modifying the alcove

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:25.924
to function as a cortical
processing subunit.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.789
That was my next guess.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.591
Then I won't need to
explain its purpose.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.426
Okay, you win.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.332
What do you do with
the cortical processing, uh...

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.801
Subunit.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.498
On Borg vessels, there's
one in each unimatrix.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.336
It downloads newly assimilated
data to the drones.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.707
But Voyager isn't a Borg vessel,

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.973
and you're not a drone anymore.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.311
Voyager collects
a great deal of information...

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.577
sensor scans,
navigational projections,

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:52.811
engineering updates,

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.946
away team reports,
scientific analyses.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.284
The results of our

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.483
Kadis-Kot tournament?

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.651
That, too.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.592
The crew must read and study
this information...

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.129
an inefficient procedure.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.166
These data nodes are downloading
the information into the alcove.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.293
Which is going to download it
into you.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.698
Precisely.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.637
In a matter of hours,
I will assimilate

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.265
several months worth of data.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.934
Can I try it sometime?

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:21.844
Your physiology is...
different from mine.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.110
Guess I'll stick
to reading my lessons

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.345
and listening
to Neelix tell stories.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.943
I will see you tomorrow.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.351
Can I watch?

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.222
Okay, tomorrow.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.555
Warning. Plate is hot.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.755
Now you tell me.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.923
You go for authenticity
and what do you get?

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.125
Second-degree burns.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.863
I've been slaving over that
replicator program for hours.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.201
What was this bizarre
rumor I heard

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:03.242
about half the crew on
Deck 5 getting pregnant?

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.776
Oh, that.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.176
The Doctor was running
generational projections

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.044
on the Sick Bay computer.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.140
Tom Paris happened
to glance at the monitor

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.912
and jumped to conclusions.

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.920
Wasn't long before
Neelix was asking me

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.922
if he could turn Cargo Bay 1
into a nursery.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.523
Word travels fast
on this ship, hmm?

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.559
Warp 10.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.790
Oh, by the way,
I meant to tell you...

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:26.491
there's a class-K nebula
25 light-years off starboard.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.726
We should take a look.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.826
A major detour
for a minor nebula.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:34.236
We are explorers, remember?

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:35.899
Permission granted.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.269
Main course,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.369
a recipe I've never tried.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.710
But we are explorers, remember?

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.617
Regeneration cycle complete.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.956
Seven of Nine
to Lieutenant Torres.

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:58.224
Lieutenant Torres, respond.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.697
Good morning, Seven.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.097
This better be important.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.499
I must speak with you at once.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.842
I'm picking up some interesting
graviton fluctuations

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.311
about ten light-years away.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.608
Can you be more specific?

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.740
Not at this distance.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:17.840
Tom...

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:18.906
alter course.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.418
I want to take
a closer look.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.114
Chakotay had his heart set
on that nebula we're headed for.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.214
He'll have to wait.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:29.421
Captain, I need permission
to shut down the sensor grid.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:33.295
Seven thinks a couple of insects
are disrupting the power flow.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.628
A mating pair

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.498
of photonic fleas,
to be more accurate

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.934
and possibly their offspring.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.938
And how did you arrive
at this theory?

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.804
Last night,
I downloaded six months

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.342
of ship status reports

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.935
into my new cortical subunit
while I was regenerating.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.604
Learn while you sleep.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.376
I tried that once...
gave me a headache.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.781
Go on.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.944
Eight weeks ago,
an away team encountered

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.818
a Kartelan freighter carrying
supplies from Sector 492,

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.790
a territory that included
a former Talaxian colony.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.827
Mr. Neelix used the opportunity

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.089
to acquire 12 kilograms
of amber spice...

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.154
a delicacy among his people.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.132
What does that have to do
with the sensor grid?

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.896
On the same day,

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.665
Ensign Kim was repairing
a replicator in the Mess Hall.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:14.604
I remember that...
Neelix told me

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.108
to stick around
to try something he was cooking.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.076
No doubt made
with the amber spice,

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.635
which contained the larvae

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.839
of the photonic fleas.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.279
How could you possibly
know that?

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:27.149
Because I also downloaded data
regarding their life cycles.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.085
The larvae flew out
of the spice jar

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.589
in search of their
primary source of nourishment...

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.090
plasma particles.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:35.286
The conduits within
the nearby sensor grid

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.727
contain an unlimited supply
of these particles.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.527
Ensign Kim had unwittingly
given the creatures access

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.033
by exposing the grid.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.932
The now mature creatures
periodically

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.834
tap into the conduit
for nourishment.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.532
When they do,
the sensor emitters

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.302
momentarily
lose their resolution.

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:52.503
A logical, though
highly speculative, analysis.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:24.304
Let's find a more
suitable home for them.

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:34.586
I'm picking up
graviton fluctuations.

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:35.848
Take us out of warp.

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.719
On screen.

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.924
Anybody want to hazard a guess?

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:45.758
They are hailing us.

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:47.424
On screen.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.797
I recommend maximum shielding.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:54.101
There are a few technical issues
I haven't worked out yet.

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.698
There's a massive graviton surge
coming from that thing.

00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:58.266
Shields to full.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.413
Your apparatus appears
to be destabilizing.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:06.179
If I don't find a way to repair
this power core, they'll be able

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.413
to see the explosion
all the way to, uh...

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.012
Where did you say you were from?

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:14.217
I didn't... but we're
from a planet called Earth.

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:16.386
All the way to... Earth.

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:18.453
Can we ask you
what it's supposed to do?

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:21.625
Catapult a vessel across space
in the time it takes to say

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.396
"catapult a vessel
across space."

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.960
Lt'll make warp drive
look like a wooden sled.

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:31.439
Maybe we can help you
with that power core.

00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:33.035
Hmm?

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:35.046
The core sends a graviton surge

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:36.706
through the projectors

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.750
which locks onto a ship

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:41.514
and sends it hurtling
into null space

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:45.284
to emerge a few hours later,
hundreds if not thousands

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:47.223
of light-years away.

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.887
I'm curious
why you built this catapult.

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:53.591
Simple... I've been looking
for a way to get home.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:54.894
We know the feeling.

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.161
I'd been exploring

00:08:56.235 --> 00:08:57.600
an unstable wormhole.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.297
Before I knew it, I was here

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:01.101
and my home planet was there.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.835
I was facing a journey
of at least ten years.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.174
Instead, I decided
to build a catapult.

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.837
Have you tested it yet?

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:09.108
Two weeks ago,

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:11.649
I sent a probe
nearly 600 light-years,

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:13.878
but it destabilized
the core.

00:09:13.986 --> 00:09:15.476
I've been trying to
fix it ever since.

00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:19.082
We can send an engineering team
over to help you.

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.523
No, no, it's too dangerous.

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.220
I wouldn't send my own crew
in there.

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:23.694
Then we could find
a way to adjust

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:24.889
the core reaction from here.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.261
A few well-timed
graviton pulses

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:27.856
from our deflector dish
might do it.

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:29.458
That's generous,

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:31.469
but I have nothing
to give in return.

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:35.098
We're not asking
for anything in return.

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:38.200
You could use the catapult
after I've made my jump.

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:40.006
It should still
be functional.

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:41.512
A thousand light-years

00:09:41.581 --> 00:09:43.811
won't exactly get
you back to Earth...

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:46.545
But it would cut a few
years off our trip.

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:48.712
If you're successful,
and if I'm satisfied

00:09:48.788 --> 00:09:50.415
a jump would be safe
for Voyager,

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:52.923
then we'll take you up
on that offer. Thank you.

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.993
Let's get started.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:38.103
Come in.

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:40.533
Good morning.

00:10:40.606 --> 00:10:41.971
Perhaps not.

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:45.077
The alien, Mr. Tash,
is trying to deceive us.

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:47.112
His catapult is the same type
of technology

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:48.703
that was used to trap Voyager

00:10:48.781 --> 00:10:50.612
in the Delta Quadrant
five years ago.

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.117
I scanned the
catapult myself.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.785
Sensors didn't pick up
anything unusual.

00:11:01.861 --> 00:11:04.762
You spent the night
in your new alcove.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.127
Processing
the same information

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:09.099
and cross-referencing it
with Voyager's database.

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:11.136
When the catapult
destabilized yesterday,

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:12.636
astrometric sensors recorded

00:11:12.705 --> 00:11:14.639
a momentary burst
of epsilon radiation.

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.335
Unusual, but not unheard of.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.900
Epsilon radiation is

00:11:18.978 --> 00:11:21.538
one the byproducts
of a tetryon reactor.

00:11:21.614 --> 00:11:23.741
According to your own entries
in the database,

00:11:23.816 --> 00:11:26.114
your only encounter
with that kind of technology

00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:27.277
occurred five years ago

00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:28.752
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:30.311
A coherent tetryon beam

00:11:30.389 --> 00:11:32.823
locked onto Voyager,
and you were hit by a massive

00:11:32.892 --> 00:11:34.792
displacement wave,
which pulled you across

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.760
70,000 light-years
in a matter of minutes.

00:11:36.829 --> 00:11:41.163
The source of that tetryon beam
was the Caretaker's Array.

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:44.134
Mr. Tash claims that his
catapult will be able to do

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:45.898
something very similar.

00:11:49.575 --> 00:11:52.635
He didn't want us
to send over a repair team.

00:11:52.712 --> 00:11:54.373
Out of concern
for our safety.

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:56.347
It's obvious he was
trying to hide

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:57.575
his tetryon reactor.

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:01.280
The first time we met
a Caretaker,

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:03.583
we were pulled
halfway across the galaxy.

00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:06.454
The second time
we were almost killed.

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:09.688
I'm not eager for a third round.

00:12:10.763 --> 00:12:12.856
Is this any way
to treat a colleague?

00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:16.026
Not so much as a molecule
of Caretaker DNA.

00:12:16.102 --> 00:12:18.764
Thank you, Doctor.

00:12:18.838 --> 00:12:21.932
There's a tetryon reactor
powering your catapult.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:26.135
You didn't want us
to find it, did you?

00:12:26.212 --> 00:12:29.648
Unless you answer my questions,
I'll resume course,

00:12:29.715 --> 00:12:32.445
and you can ask
somebody else for help.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:36.147
Look, I acquired the tetryon
reactor at great cost.

00:12:36.222 --> 00:12:38.554
This territory is
full of species

00:12:38.624 --> 00:12:42.287
who would do anything for
such advanced technology,

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:43.828
including steal it.

00:12:45.097 --> 00:12:46.962
I apologize for the deception,

00:12:47.032 --> 00:12:48.829
but you do understand.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.865
We made an agreement
to cooperate.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.964
I see no reason
not to continue.

00:12:56.075 --> 00:12:57.542
Thank you, Captain.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:59.737
Keep me informed
on your progress.

00:13:00.913 --> 00:13:02.676
That reactor had
to come from somewhere.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:04.306
I can't just ignore
the possibility

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:05.680
of a Caretaker nearby.

00:13:05.751 --> 00:13:06.718
Keep scanning.

00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:07.844
See what you can find.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.410
There is another
possibility.

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.388
The reactor may have come
from the same Array

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:13.322
that brought Voyager
to the Delta Quadrant.

00:13:13.392 --> 00:13:15.019
That's a long shot, Seven.

00:13:15.094 --> 00:13:16.186
Maybe not.

00:13:16.262 --> 00:13:18.162
Again, according to your
own reports, you believed

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.595
the only way
to keep the Array

00:13:19.665 --> 00:13:21.758
from falling
into the wrong hands

00:13:21.834 --> 00:13:22.926
was to destroy it.

00:13:23.068 --> 00:13:24.160
It's possible

00:13:24.236 --> 00:13:26.067
the destruction
was incomplete.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:29.938
And one of the reactors
survived?

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:31.942
We scanned for debris.

00:13:32.077 --> 00:13:35.911
There was nothing left but some
fused pieces of metal alloy.

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:38.347
I wish to reexamine the sensor
records from that event.

00:13:38.417 --> 00:13:39.850
In case we were mistaken.

00:13:39.919 --> 00:13:41.045
Yes.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.350
Go right ahead.

00:13:43.422 --> 00:13:45.754
Computer,
describe the debris remaining

00:13:45.825 --> 00:13:47.952
after the Array was destroyed.

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:50.552
Particulate dust
and metallic fragments

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:52.961
composed of an unknown alloy,

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:56.195
vapor composed of hydrogen,
helium, mercury and argon.

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:58.862
Was there anything left
of the tetryon reactor?

00:13:58.938 --> 00:14:00.235
Negative.

00:14:00.306 --> 00:14:04.003
Specify the yield
of the tricobalt device.

00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:06.408
20,000 teracochranes.

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:08.275
Who programmed the device?

00:14:08.347 --> 00:14:09.473
Commander Tuvok.

00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:12.449
Display the detonation.

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:18.089
Advance the image
by.01 seconds.

00:14:18.157 --> 00:14:19.556
Again.

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:24.325
Isolate grid 3-7 and magnify.

00:14:26.932 --> 00:14:28.559
Is that a tractor beam?

00:14:28.634 --> 00:14:30.469
Insufficient sensor data.

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:32.936
Identify its source.

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:35.472
Insufficient sensor data.

00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:39.102
Identify the isolated section
of the Array.

00:14:39.178 --> 00:14:40.941
Secondary power core.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.641
Which contained
a tetryon reactor.

00:14:44.717 --> 00:14:46.810
Affirmative.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.951
Commander, I've been
reviewing the data

00:14:54.093 --> 00:14:56.653
on the destruction
of the Caretaker's Array.

00:14:56.729 --> 00:14:59.630
Unfortunately, the sensor
records are incomplete.

00:14:59.698 --> 00:15:00.756
I don't doubt it.

00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:02.733
We were being attacked
by the Kazon.

00:15:02.801 --> 00:15:04.701
Half the ship's
systems were down.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:05.702
A single Kazon vessel.

00:15:05.771 --> 00:15:08.296
Armed to the teeth.

00:15:08.374 --> 00:15:10.467
Commander, you fired
the tricobalt charge

00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:11.804
that destroyed the Array.

00:15:11.877 --> 00:15:12.809
Correct.

00:15:12.878 --> 00:15:14.277
Under the Captain's orders?

00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:17.372
Did you also program
the charge?

00:15:17.449 --> 00:15:18.780
Yes.

00:15:18.851 --> 00:15:20.546
Under the Captain's orders
as well?

00:15:20.619 --> 00:15:21.779
Not directly.

00:15:21.854 --> 00:15:24.015
I determined the yield.

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:25.716
20,000 teracochranes.

00:15:25.791 --> 00:15:26.917
That's correct.

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:28.788
According to sensor estimates

00:15:28.861 --> 00:15:31.557
of the Array's hull integrity,
a charge of half that yield

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.325
would have been
sufficient.

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:36.596
The Captain wanted nothing left
for the Kazon to use.

00:15:36.669 --> 00:15:39.866
I calculated a yield
certain to produce that result.

00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:41.873
Something may have
escaped the blast...

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.465
one of the tetryon reactors.

00:15:43.542 --> 00:15:45.533
But we scanned for debris.

00:15:45.611 --> 00:15:49.172
The charge you detonated
tore an opening in subspace.

00:15:49.248 --> 00:15:51.648
And that's where
the reactor went?

00:15:51.717 --> 00:15:52.945
Yes.

00:15:53.085 --> 00:15:54.882
How?

00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:57.252
It was pushed there
by a tractor beam.

00:15:57.323 --> 00:15:58.722
Do you have evidence

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:00.918
of a tractor beam?

00:16:00.993 --> 00:16:02.483
Perhaps.

00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:05.359
Speculation is not evidence.

00:16:05.431 --> 00:16:07.023
There was no tractor beam,

00:16:07.099 --> 00:16:10.193
because there was no ship
in the vicinity to generate one,

00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:12.260
unless you can prove otherwise.

00:16:12.338 --> 00:16:15.466
Thank you, Commander.

00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:38.296
Looking for a midnight snack?

00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:39.558
I require information.

00:16:39.631 --> 00:16:40.757
I'm attempting to determine

00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:42.164
whether the
catapult technology

00:16:42.234 --> 00:16:43.929
was derived from
the Caretaker's Array.

00:16:44.036 --> 00:16:44.934
So I heard.

00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:47.232
A fascinating theory.

00:16:47.306 --> 00:16:49.274
It's got my mind spinning.

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:51.241
How long were you
in the vicinity of the Array

00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:52.538
before Voyager arrived?

00:16:52.611 --> 00:16:53.578
About a year.

00:16:53.645 --> 00:16:55.704
Kes was on a nearby planet

00:16:55.781 --> 00:16:58.716
and, uh, we were
getting very close.

00:16:58.784 --> 00:16:59.944
Did you ever encounter

00:17:00.085 --> 00:17:01.416
the Caretaker directly?

00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:02.886
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:05.753
In my opinion, any being
powerful enough to grab ships

00:17:05.824 --> 00:17:08.554
from the other side
of the galaxy should be avoided.

00:17:08.627 --> 00:17:10.117
According to
Voyager's database,

00:17:10.195 --> 00:17:11.423
he claimed he was searching

00:17:11.497 --> 00:17:13.089
for a genetically
compatible mate.

00:17:13.165 --> 00:17:14.723
Did you believe
that explanation?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.291
I had no reason to doubt it,

00:17:17.369 --> 00:17:20.463
though it did seem
a bit excessive.

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:21.631
I mean, all those ships.

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:22.901
What happened to them?

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:24.602
Well, after he sampled
the crew's DNA,

00:17:24.676 --> 00:17:26.268
he sent them back
where they came from

00:17:26.345 --> 00:17:27.471
I suppose.

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:28.911
You know, Kes always thought

00:17:29.048 --> 00:17:32.040
something more was going on,

00:17:32.117 --> 00:17:34.813
but she had
quite an imagination.

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:37.082
Were there any other ships
in the area

00:17:37.156 --> 00:17:38.487
after Voyager arrived?

00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:39.489
Only the Kazon.

00:17:39.558 --> 00:17:40.650
But the Caretaker

00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:42.023
could have pulled in

00:17:42.094 --> 00:17:44.358
another vessel...
a cloaked ship, perhaps.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:46.091
Seven, what are you getting at?

00:17:46.165 --> 00:17:47.257
A third ship hidden

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:48.856
from both Voyager and the Kazon.

00:17:48.934 --> 00:17:51.767
What was it doing there?

00:17:51.837 --> 00:17:55.034
Preventing the tetryon reactor
from being destroyed.

00:17:55.107 --> 00:17:57.234
Kes was right.

00:17:57.309 --> 00:18:00.710
Something was going on.

00:18:00.779 --> 00:18:03.009
Voyager's sensor logs were
damaged in the Kazon attack.

00:18:03.082 --> 00:18:04.049
I can't be certain.

00:18:04.116 --> 00:18:07.108
Maybe I can help.

00:18:07.186 --> 00:18:08.813
The sensor records
off my ship

00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:09.979
weren't damaged.

00:18:10.055 --> 00:18:11.522
I can give them to you.

00:18:35.747 --> 00:18:37.578
The tetryon reaction is stable.

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:40.516
Graviton field is set
for a 100 light-year jump.

00:18:40.586 --> 00:18:42.520
The catapult's locking on
to him.

00:18:42.588 --> 00:18:43.919
We're being hailed.

00:18:43.989 --> 00:18:45.354
On screen.

00:18:45.424 --> 00:18:49.724
I'll contact you the moment
I reenter normal space.

00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:51.023
Thank you, Captain.

00:18:51.096 --> 00:18:52.723
My pleasure.

00:18:52.798 --> 00:18:54.095
Catapult is at full power.

00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:55.793
Good-bye to you all.

00:18:57.402 --> 00:19:00.394
Final launch sequence
has been initiated.

00:19:11.817 --> 00:19:12.875
He's gone.

00:19:13.018 --> 00:19:14.747
How long before we can expect

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.082
to hear from him?

00:19:16.155 --> 00:19:18.589
If his vessel survived,
one or two hours.

00:19:18.657 --> 00:19:19.624
Seven of Nine

00:19:19.691 --> 00:19:21.215
to Commander Chakotay.

00:19:21.293 --> 00:19:22.521
Go ahead.

00:19:22.594 --> 00:19:25.893
I require your assistance
in the Astrometrics Lab.

00:19:25.964 --> 00:19:27.864
On my way.

00:19:31.403 --> 00:19:32.870
Computer, seal the doors.

00:19:32.938 --> 00:19:35.406
Deactivate all sensors
within this room.

00:19:35.474 --> 00:19:36.441
Acknowledged.

00:19:36.508 --> 00:19:37.873
What's this about?

00:19:37.943 --> 00:19:40.776
I believe Voyager's presence
in the Delta Quadrant

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:42.211
is no accident.

00:19:42.281 --> 00:19:44.875
You and the crew have been
stranded here intentionally.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.884
By whom?

00:19:46.952 --> 00:19:48.783
Captain Janeway.

00:19:52.791 --> 00:19:54.588
The Captain and Tuvok
were involved

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:56.127
in a Federation conspiracy.

00:19:56.195 --> 00:19:58.425
They're in collusion
with the Caretaker

00:19:58.497 --> 00:20:00.124
and possibly
the Cardassians.

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:01.826
I see.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.562
And the point
of this conspiracy?

00:20:04.636 --> 00:20:06.331
I believe
they're attempting to establish

00:20:06.405 --> 00:20:08.168
a military presence
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.571
That's quite a theory.

00:20:09.641 --> 00:20:11.506
Perhaps you haven't heard
of the Jankata Accord.

00:20:11.577 --> 00:20:13.670
"No species shall
enter another Quadrant

00:20:13.745 --> 00:20:15.940
for the purpose
of territorial expansion."

00:20:16.048 --> 00:20:18.778
The Federation signed it,
the Cardassians signed it,

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:22.081
and Captain Janeway would be
the last person to violate it.

00:20:22.154 --> 00:20:23.485
Improbable as it may sound,

00:20:23.555 --> 00:20:25.682
I've found compelling evidence

00:20:25.757 --> 00:20:27.281
to support my theory.

00:20:27.359 --> 00:20:29.122
What kind of evidence?

00:20:29.194 --> 00:20:32.163
I've analyzed over 30 million
teraquads of data

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:33.664
regarding Voyager's
activities

00:20:33.732 --> 00:20:34.960
over the past five years.

00:20:35.033 --> 00:20:36.466
It's quite clear

00:20:36.535 --> 00:20:38.969
that we've been the victim
of an elaborate deception.

00:20:39.104 --> 00:20:41.902
I don't have the benefit
of a cortical processor.

00:20:41.974 --> 00:20:44.465
Why don't you give me
the abridged version?

00:20:44.543 --> 00:20:46.943
In the months
before Voyager's arrival,

00:20:47.012 --> 00:20:48.809
Neelix recorded
the appearance

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:51.007
of 52 vessels,
including this one.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.118
A Cardassian warship.

00:20:54.186 --> 00:20:56.984
A remarkable coincidence.

00:20:57.089 --> 00:20:58.886
Only days
before Voyager's arrival,

00:20:58.957 --> 00:21:01.721
the Cardassians were already
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:21:01.793 --> 00:21:04.626
The Caretaker was trying
to find a mate, remember?

00:21:04.696 --> 00:21:07.324
He was pulling ships
from all over the galaxy.

00:21:07.399 --> 00:21:09.560
I'm familiar
with the Caretaker's actions.

00:21:09.635 --> 00:21:12.229
In each instance,
he would examine the crew's DNA

00:21:12.304 --> 00:21:14.499
and when he failed
to find a genetic match,

00:21:14.573 --> 00:21:17.133
he would release the vessel,
but in this instance,

00:21:17.209 --> 00:21:19.473
Neelix's sensors indicated
the ship vanished.

00:21:19.544 --> 00:21:20.875
Obviously, it was returned

00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.208
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:21:22.281 --> 00:21:23.373
Why?

00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:25.416
You seem to have
all the answers.

00:21:25.484 --> 00:21:27.111
I believe the Cardassians
were sent back

00:21:27.185 --> 00:21:28.516
to deliver strategic information

00:21:28.587 --> 00:21:30.555
regarding the Delta Quadrant.

00:21:30.622 --> 00:21:31.748
Conjecture.

00:21:31.823 --> 00:21:33.085
Extrapolation.

00:21:33.158 --> 00:21:34.819
I can believe the Cardassians

00:21:34.893 --> 00:21:37.088
might be involved in this,
but not Starfleet.

00:21:37.162 --> 00:21:38.527
There are precedents

00:21:38.597 --> 00:21:41.327
for unauthorized missions
of this type, Commander.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.391
According
to the Federation database,

00:21:43.468 --> 00:21:45.936
the Maquis were victims
of several of them.

00:21:48.907 --> 00:21:51.205
All right,
you've got my attention.

00:21:51.276 --> 00:21:54.905
You said that Tuvok and
Captain Janeway were involved.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.242
Tell me how.

00:21:56.315 --> 00:21:57.748
At the same time

00:21:57.816 --> 00:21:59.750
the Cardassians were meeting
with the Caretaker,

00:21:59.818 --> 00:22:01.376
your Maquis vessel
was infiltrated

00:22:01.453 --> 00:22:03.045
with a Starfleet agent.

00:22:03.121 --> 00:22:04.247
Tuvok.

00:22:04.323 --> 00:22:05.915
Your navigator.

00:22:05.991 --> 00:22:07.151
He guided your ship

00:22:07.225 --> 00:22:09.420
to prearranged coordinates
in the Badlands,

00:22:09.494 --> 00:22:11.394
where the Caretaker
locked onto you.

00:22:11.463 --> 00:22:13.795
Once you were pulled
into the Delta Quadrant

00:22:13.865 --> 00:22:15.662
Tuvok could've
secretly transmitted

00:22:15.734 --> 00:22:17.634
final instructions
to the Caretaker.

00:22:17.703 --> 00:22:20.331
A short time later,
Captain Janeway guided Voyager

00:22:20.405 --> 00:22:21.599
to the same coordinates

00:22:21.673 --> 00:22:23.937
and was also pulled
into the Delta Quadrant.

00:22:24.076 --> 00:22:26.840
All of these events took place
within a matter of days.

00:22:26.912 --> 00:22:28.277
I find that suspicious.

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:31.316
I'll admit, the timing seems
a little convenient,

00:22:31.383 --> 00:22:34.079
but that doesn't mean
there was a master plan.

00:22:34.152 --> 00:22:37.644
Why did the Captain
destroy the Array?

00:22:37.723 --> 00:22:40.658
So the Kazon couldn't use it
to attack the Ocampa.

00:22:40.726 --> 00:22:43.354
That's what she told the crew,
but I believe she intended

00:22:43.428 --> 00:22:45.362
to remain
in the Delta Quadrant all along.

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:46.897
If the Array
had remained intact,

00:22:46.965 --> 00:22:49.490
you and all the others
would have insisted on using it

00:22:49.568 --> 00:22:50.592
to return home.

00:22:50.669 --> 00:22:52.296
She was keeping it
from the Kazon.

00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:54.737
The Captain ordered
Commander Tuvok

00:22:54.806 --> 00:22:56.398
to destroy the Array.

00:22:56.475 --> 00:22:58.170
He fired
two tricobalt devices.

00:23:01.847 --> 00:23:04.145
Are those weapons
normally carried

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:05.911
on Federation starships?

00:23:05.984 --> 00:23:07.144
No.

00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:09.687
Yet they were part
of Voyager's arsenal.

00:23:09.755 --> 00:23:10.687
Why?

00:23:10.756 --> 00:23:12.690
I can't explain that.

00:23:12.758 --> 00:23:14.020
I can.

00:23:14.092 --> 00:23:15.855
Neither phasers nor torpedoes

00:23:15.927 --> 00:23:18.122
are capable
of creating a tear in subspace.

00:23:18.196 --> 00:23:19.720
A tricobalt device is.

00:23:19.798 --> 00:23:23.666
As Tuvok detonated the device,
a cloaked ship locked on

00:23:23.735 --> 00:23:25.930
to one of the Array's
tetryon reactors

00:23:26.004 --> 00:23:26.936
and pushed it

00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:28.869
through the tear into subspace,

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:30.635
protecting it from the blast,

00:23:30.709 --> 00:23:33.109
and hiding it
from Voyager's sensors...

00:23:33.178 --> 00:23:34.941
but the Captain and Tuvok knew

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:36.707
exactly where it was going.

00:23:36.782 --> 00:23:38.340
Once Voyager left the area,

00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:40.647
the reactor was retrieved

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:41.947
and began a similar journey

00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:43.554
carried by a series of vessels,

00:23:43.622 --> 00:23:45.783
until it was finally
delivered to Mr. Tash.

00:23:45.857 --> 00:23:48.690
Who used it
to build the catapult.

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:50.557
He was waiting here for Voyager

00:23:50.629 --> 00:23:52.961
and for the final phase
of the mission.

00:23:53.064 --> 00:23:55.498
Which is what, exactly?

00:23:55.567 --> 00:23:57.501
I don't think
Captain Janeway is planning

00:23:57.569 --> 00:23:59.969
to use the catapult
to get Voyager closer to home.

00:24:00.071 --> 00:24:02.699
I think she's going to use it
to bring in more vessels

00:24:02.774 --> 00:24:04.537
from the Alpha Quadrant.

00:24:04.609 --> 00:24:06.008
If I'm correct,

00:24:06.077 --> 00:24:08.238
this region of space
will soon be occupied

00:24:08.313 --> 00:24:10.543
by a Federation-Cardassian
invasion force.

00:24:10.615 --> 00:24:11.547
You've uncovered

00:24:11.616 --> 00:24:12.878
some interesting facts,

00:24:12.951 --> 00:24:15.249
but your interpretation
is farfetched.

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:16.844
These are random incidents.

00:24:16.922 --> 00:24:19.356
Granted, some of them
are hard to explain,

00:24:19.424 --> 00:24:21.221
but there's no conspiracy here.

00:24:21.293 --> 00:24:24.820
Stardate 51008.

00:24:24.896 --> 00:24:27.023
Captain Janeway allows Kes
to leave Voyager.

00:24:27.098 --> 00:24:28.827
Neelix told me
that Kes had suspicions

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:30.128
about the Caretaker.

00:24:30.202 --> 00:24:32.466
Was the Captain trying
to silence her?

00:24:32.537 --> 00:24:34.095
Stardate 51462.

00:24:34.172 --> 00:24:35.764
The Doctor's program
is transmitted

00:24:35.841 --> 00:24:36.808
to a Starfleet vessel

00:24:36.875 --> 00:24:38.672
on the outskirts
of the Alpha Quadrant...

00:24:38.743 --> 00:24:40.233
an attempt by the Captain
to contact Earth,

00:24:40.312 --> 00:24:41.939
or a secret communiqué

00:24:42.080 --> 00:24:43.945
informing Starfleet
of her progress?

00:24:44.015 --> 00:24:46.176
Stardate 50984.

00:24:46.251 --> 00:24:48.481
Janeway forges an alliance
with the Borg.

00:24:48.553 --> 00:24:52.080
Stardate 51762.
A cease-fire with the Hirogen.

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:53.647
Stardate 52861.

00:24:53.725 --> 00:24:56.125
A non-aggression pact
with the Terkellian.

00:24:56.194 --> 00:24:58.754
She called each incident,
"diplomacy."

00:24:58.830 --> 00:24:59.762
I believe she was trying

00:24:59.831 --> 00:25:01.890
to establish
a tactical infrastructure

00:25:02.033 --> 00:25:03.057
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:25:03.134 --> 00:25:04.294
Over the past five years,

00:25:04.369 --> 00:25:06.701
Captain Janeway
has altered course 263

00:25:06.771 --> 00:25:08.636
times
in the name of exploration.

00:25:08.707 --> 00:25:11.039
In reality, she was mapping
the region and collecting

00:25:11.109 --> 00:25:12.167
strategic data regarding...

00:25:12.244 --> 00:25:13.438
I get the point.

00:25:13.512 --> 00:25:16.140
You still doubt my suspicions,

00:25:16.214 --> 00:25:18.614
but can you be certain
I'm wrong?

00:25:18.683 --> 00:25:20.310
Absolutely certain?

00:25:22.988 --> 00:25:24.046
No.

00:25:24.122 --> 00:25:25.646
Until you are,

00:25:25.724 --> 00:25:27.555
you mustn't allow
Captain Janeway

00:25:27.626 --> 00:25:29.594
to retain control
of the catapult.

00:25:40.171 --> 00:25:43.163
I'm picking up a transmission,
heavily distorted.

00:25:43.241 --> 00:25:44.469
He made it.

00:25:44.543 --> 00:25:46.670
Can you clear it up?

00:25:48.346 --> 00:25:49.643
Success, Captain...

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:51.477
5,000 light-years.

00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:53.484
Are you all right?

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:56.043
A few systems overloaded...
nothing serious.

00:25:56.121 --> 00:25:58.954
I had to readjust my shields
during mid-flight...

00:25:59.024 --> 00:26:00.582
almost lost my outer hull.

00:26:00.659 --> 00:26:02.889
I'm sending you
the modifications.

00:26:03.028 --> 00:26:04.893
My catapult is yours, Captain.

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:05.930
Good luck.

00:26:08.099 --> 00:26:09.828
Get that data down to B'Elanna.

00:26:09.901 --> 00:26:10.833
Tell her

00:26:10.902 --> 00:26:12.164
to enhance our shields.

00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:14.569
So we're going ahead
with the jump?

00:26:14.639 --> 00:26:16.664
I want to run
a few more tests,

00:26:16.741 --> 00:26:18.038
launch some probes,

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:20.134
but if it all checks out,
I see no reason not to.

00:26:20.211 --> 00:26:21.906
I've received

00:26:22.047 --> 00:26:23.036
the telemetry.

00:26:23.114 --> 00:26:24.945
I'll take it to Engineering.

00:26:31.990 --> 00:26:33.924
I want you to add
a.03 variance

00:26:34.059 --> 00:26:35.924
to these shield
modifications.

00:26:35.994 --> 00:26:37.757
That'll disrupt
the emitters.

00:26:37.829 --> 00:26:39.694
And you'll need
another six hours

00:26:39.764 --> 00:26:41.595
to get them back
on line, I know.

00:26:41.666 --> 00:26:43.600
Have you run this
by the Captain?

00:26:43.668 --> 00:26:44.760
No...

00:26:44.836 --> 00:26:46.428
and I'm not going to...

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:48.768
not yet.

00:26:54.412 --> 00:26:55.674
She's pulling your leg.

00:26:55.747 --> 00:26:59.615
It-it's got to be some kind
of Borg practical joke.

00:27:00.986 --> 00:27:02.078
She wasn't joking.

00:27:02.153 --> 00:27:03.245
A secret mission?

00:27:03.321 --> 00:27:05.755
Starfleet in league
with the Caretaker?

00:27:05.824 --> 00:27:07.621
It's ridiculous.

00:27:09.761 --> 00:27:10.853
"Ridiculous"?

00:27:10.929 --> 00:27:12.760
Seven has some
compelling evidence.

00:27:12.831 --> 00:27:14.389
Well, then,
let's go to the Captain,

00:27:14.466 --> 00:27:15.398
get a straight answer.

00:27:15.467 --> 00:27:16.661
"Good morning, Kathryn.

00:27:16.735 --> 00:27:18.168
"All systems are operational.

00:27:18.236 --> 00:27:19.794
"The crew's in good health.

00:27:19.871 --> 00:27:21.133
"And by the way, is it true

00:27:21.206 --> 00:27:23.265
you've been lying
to us for five years?"

00:27:29.681 --> 00:27:32.275
I'm not prepared
to make that accusation,

00:27:32.350 --> 00:27:34.978
but I can't ignore
what I've heard, either.

00:27:39.024 --> 00:27:40.616
So, what do you suggest?

00:27:40.692 --> 00:27:43.490
I want you to delay
those shield modifications.

00:27:43.561 --> 00:27:46.655
That'll give me time
to check Seven's database,

00:27:46.731 --> 00:27:48.824
take a look
at the evidence myself.

00:27:51.369 --> 00:27:53.735
The Captain asked me
to work with you on the shields.

00:27:53.805 --> 00:27:55.568
That won't be
necessary, Ensign.

00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:56.937
Oh, I don't mind.

00:27:57.042 --> 00:27:59.135
Oh, you know how eager she is
to make that jump.

00:27:59.210 --> 00:28:00.507
Harry, we're fine here.

00:28:02.213 --> 00:28:03.305
"Too many cooks," Harry.

00:28:03.381 --> 00:28:04.643
You know how it is.

00:28:04.716 --> 00:28:06.946
We'll let you know
when we're done.

00:28:13.692 --> 00:28:16.286
Download complete.

00:28:20.331 --> 00:28:22.322
Seven of Nine
to Captain Janeway.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:23.594
Go ahead.

00:28:23.668 --> 00:28:26.660
I need to speak with you
in the Astrometrics Lab.

00:28:26.738 --> 00:28:27.864
I'm on my way.

00:28:33.178 --> 00:28:34.406
Computer, seal the door

00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:36.913
and deactivate internal sensors
to this room.

00:28:37.015 --> 00:28:37.913
Acknowledged.

00:28:38.016 --> 00:28:38.914
Seven?

00:28:39.050 --> 00:28:40.176
I believe Chakotay

00:28:40.251 --> 00:28:42.446
and other members
of your crew are involved

00:28:42.520 --> 00:28:43.919
in a conspiracy to resurrect

00:28:44.022 --> 00:28:45.114
the Maquis Rebellion.

00:28:45.190 --> 00:28:47.385
Did Chakotay put
you up to this?

00:28:47.459 --> 00:28:50.121
Voyager and the
Federation itself

00:28:50.195 --> 00:28:51.219
are in grave danger.

00:28:51.296 --> 00:28:52.388
Go on.

00:28:52.464 --> 00:28:54.227
I've concluded
that Chakotay intends

00:28:54.299 --> 00:28:56.267
to use the catapult
to launch attacks

00:28:56.334 --> 00:28:58.734
against Cardassian
and Federation starships.

00:28:58.803 --> 00:29:00.464
Chakotay gave up his allegiance

00:29:00.538 --> 00:29:02.199
to the Maquis a long time ago.

00:29:02.273 --> 00:29:03.638
What you're saying
makes no sense.

00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:04.640
Improbable as it may sound,

00:29:04.709 --> 00:29:06.870
I found
compelling evidence

00:29:07.011 --> 00:29:09.275
to support my theory.

00:29:09.347 --> 00:29:12.043
In the months
before Voyager's arrival,

00:29:12.117 --> 00:29:14.745
Neelix recorded
the sudden appearance

00:29:14.819 --> 00:29:17.413
of 52 vessels...
including this one.

00:29:17.489 --> 00:29:20.822
A Cardassian warship.

00:29:20.892 --> 00:29:23.190
I've analyzed the hull geometry
and warp signature.

00:29:23.261 --> 00:29:24.489
It was one
of the same ships

00:29:24.562 --> 00:29:26.325
that were pursuing Chakotay
and his crew

00:29:26.397 --> 00:29:28.092
in the region known
as the Badlands.

00:29:28.166 --> 00:29:29.827
It was pulled
into the Delta Quadrant

00:29:29.901 --> 00:29:31.698
by the Caretaker
during that engagement.

00:29:31.770 --> 00:29:33.328
According
to Federation records,

00:29:33.404 --> 00:29:35.895
that same Cardassian warship
was found destroyed

00:29:36.007 --> 00:29:37.099
in the Badlands.

00:29:37.175 --> 00:29:38.506
The investigation revealed

00:29:38.576 --> 00:29:40.373
that it was attacked
by the Maquis.

00:29:40.445 --> 00:29:42.140
I believe that for
some unknown reason

00:29:42.213 --> 00:29:43.612
the Caretaker had
sent this ship

00:29:43.681 --> 00:29:44.875
back to the Alpha Quadrant,

00:29:44.949 --> 00:29:47.179
and that Commander Chakotay
attacked the vessel

00:29:47.252 --> 00:29:49.049
before it could reach
its destination.

00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:50.553
He downloaded its computer core

00:29:50.622 --> 00:29:53.182
and discovered the presence
of the Caretaker's Array.

00:29:53.258 --> 00:29:55.249
He realized that the
Array could be used

00:29:55.326 --> 00:29:56.588
by the Maquis as a weapon

00:29:56.661 --> 00:29:58.629
to launch surprise attacks
against Cardassian

00:29:58.696 --> 00:29:59.754
and Starfleet vessels.

00:30:01.833 --> 00:30:04.734
Well, I commend you
for your imagination,

00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:07.567
but Tuvok was a spy
on Chakotay's ship.

00:30:07.639 --> 00:30:09.436
If your theory were true,

00:30:09.507 --> 00:30:11.532
he would have
known about it.

00:30:11.609 --> 00:30:12.541
He does.

00:30:12.610 --> 00:30:14.771
Tuvok has been
collaborating

00:30:14.846 --> 00:30:16.643
with the Maquis resistance
all along.

00:30:16.714 --> 00:30:18.045
That's not possible, Seven.

00:30:18.116 --> 00:30:19.276
With Tuvok's assistance,

00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:20.612
Chakotay plotted a course

00:30:20.685 --> 00:30:22.380
toward the next
likely appearance

00:30:22.453 --> 00:30:24.284
of the Caretaker's
displacement wave

00:30:24.355 --> 00:30:25.822
offering his vessel as bait.

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:27.187
His ploy almost succeeded,

00:30:27.258 --> 00:30:29.055
but the Caretaker was
more powerful

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:30.151
than he anticipated.

00:30:30.228 --> 00:30:31.957
His crew was taken captive.

00:30:32.096 --> 00:30:34.496
A few days later,
Voyager arrived

00:30:34.566 --> 00:30:35.965
and facilitated their escape.

00:30:36.034 --> 00:30:37.558
Chakotay seized that opportunity

00:30:37.635 --> 00:30:40.195
to make one last attempt
to gain control of the Array,

00:30:40.271 --> 00:30:42.398
but, then, you gave the order
to destroy it.

00:30:42.473 --> 00:30:45.738
Circumstantial evidence...
not proof.

00:30:45.810 --> 00:30:48.278
Who carried out your order
to destroy the Array?

00:30:48.346 --> 00:30:49.278
Tuvok.

00:30:49.347 --> 00:30:50.541
Using what type
of technology?

00:30:50.615 --> 00:30:51.980
Tricobalt devices.

00:30:53.351 --> 00:30:55.945
He set the yield
to 20,000 teracochranes.

00:30:56.020 --> 00:30:57.988
It was enough
to tear an opening

00:30:58.056 --> 00:30:58.988
in subspace.

00:30:59.057 --> 00:31:00.581
A cloaked ship locked on

00:31:00.658 --> 00:31:02.148
to one of the reactors,
protecting it

00:31:02.227 --> 00:31:04.855
from the blast and hiding it
from Voyager's sensors.

00:31:04.929 --> 00:31:06.191
The reactor was retrieved

00:31:06.264 --> 00:31:07.925
and carried
by a series of vessels,

00:31:08.032 --> 00:31:09.897
until it was delivered
to Mr. Tash,

00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:11.765
who was well-compensated
by Chakotay

00:31:11.836 --> 00:31:13.326
to build the catapult.

00:31:13.404 --> 00:31:16.737
He was waiting here for Voyager,
so Chakotay could complete

00:31:16.808 --> 00:31:19.868
the mission he was forced
to abandon five years ago.

00:31:21.279 --> 00:31:25.306
I'd be willing to consider
this theory of yours...

00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:28.819
if I didn't know Chakotay
as well as I do.

00:31:28.887 --> 00:31:32.345
There is no one on this ship
I trust more.

00:31:34.392 --> 00:31:35.950
What you've done here

00:31:36.060 --> 00:31:37.960
is build what we call
a house of cards.

00:31:38.096 --> 00:31:40.564
Stardate 48658.

00:31:40.632 --> 00:31:43.795
Commander Seska is revealed
to be a Cardassian spy.

00:31:43.868 --> 00:31:45.358
She defects to the Kazon

00:31:45.436 --> 00:31:48.132
and impregnates herself
with Chakotay's DNA.

00:31:48.206 --> 00:31:50.470
Was he unaware of the procedure,
as he claims,

00:31:50.541 --> 00:31:51.974
or were they working together

00:31:52.043 --> 00:31:54.341
to create a new Kazon sect
to capture Voyager?

00:31:54.412 --> 00:31:55.436
Stardate 49522.

00:31:55.513 --> 00:31:57.743
Chakotay recommends
establishing

00:31:57.815 --> 00:31:59.976
trade relations
with the Kolhari.

00:32:00.084 --> 00:32:02.416
Their technology uses
tetryon power cells.

00:32:02.487 --> 00:32:03.920
A simple diplomatic
overture,

00:32:04.022 --> 00:32:07.321
or was he seeking a source
of energy for the catapult?

00:32:07.392 --> 00:32:09.257
Stardate 49571...

00:32:21.372 --> 00:32:23.203
Seven.

00:32:23.274 --> 00:32:24.673
Naomi Wildman.

00:32:24.742 --> 00:32:25.800
Where are you going?

00:32:25.877 --> 00:32:27.469
That's not your concern.

00:32:27.545 --> 00:32:29.012
What's wrong?

00:32:30.915 --> 00:32:32.644
Your father was Ktarian.

00:32:32.717 --> 00:32:34.241
So?

00:32:34.319 --> 00:32:36.844
The Ktarians were officially
with the Federation,

00:32:36.921 --> 00:32:38.855
but they sympathized
with the Maquis.

00:32:38.923 --> 00:32:40.550
What are you talking about?

00:32:40.625 --> 00:32:42.957
Who are you working for,
Chakotay or the Captain?

00:32:43.061 --> 00:32:44.585
Seven...

00:32:44.662 --> 00:32:46.220
Tell them it's too late.

00:32:46.297 --> 00:32:47.264
Go!

00:32:58.309 --> 00:33:02.211
I picked up a power surge
coming from the Cargo Bay.

00:33:02.280 --> 00:33:04.180
I detected the same thing.

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:06.239
You think it's the
enhanced alcove?

00:33:06.317 --> 00:33:07.443
Could be.

00:33:07.518 --> 00:33:08.678
Let's take a look.

00:33:10.722 --> 00:33:13.919
Are phasers standard
equipment on board now?

00:33:13.992 --> 00:33:16.256
Must be.

00:33:16.327 --> 00:33:18.921
The data buffer's
been activated.

00:33:18.997 --> 00:33:20.259
I wanted to make sure

00:33:20.331 --> 00:33:21.923
it wasn't malfunctioning.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:23.433
Well, you should be careful.

00:33:23.501 --> 00:33:27.130
Somebody might think you were
trying to delete a few files.

00:33:27.205 --> 00:33:30.197
Why would they think that?

00:33:30.274 --> 00:33:32.435
Some of those files
could contain

00:33:32.510 --> 00:33:33.943
sensitive information.

00:33:34.045 --> 00:33:36.479
If that's true,
somebody might think

00:33:36.547 --> 00:33:39.038
you were trying to do
the same thing.

00:33:39.117 --> 00:33:41.210
That catapult out there...

00:33:41.285 --> 00:33:44.254
it's a powerful piece
of technology.

00:33:44.322 --> 00:33:48.554
If the Maquis ever had access
to something like it,

00:33:48.626 --> 00:33:51.094
they might
have been successful.

00:33:51.162 --> 00:33:54.325
And if we had, your mission
to the Delta Quadrant

00:33:54.399 --> 00:33:56.731
never would have gotten
off the drawing board.

00:33:56.801 --> 00:33:58.564
What are you talking about?

00:33:58.636 --> 00:34:00.263
The mission you've been on

00:34:00.338 --> 00:34:01.999
for the last five years.

00:34:02.073 --> 00:34:05.133
My only mission
is trying to get Voyager home.

00:34:05.209 --> 00:34:06.767
Seven showed me
the sensor records.

00:34:06.844 --> 00:34:08.106
I saw the tractor beam.

00:34:08.179 --> 00:34:09.840
She showed me the same thing,

00:34:09.914 --> 00:34:12.007
but she implicated you

00:34:12.083 --> 00:34:14.313
in some kind of Maquis plot.

00:34:19.023 --> 00:34:20.456
Same evidence.

00:34:20.525 --> 00:34:23.255
Two different theories.

00:34:23.327 --> 00:34:25.921
It all started
with those damn photonic fleas.

00:34:26.030 --> 00:34:28.464
She was downloading
Voyager's database...

00:34:28.533 --> 00:34:30.057
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:34:30.134 --> 00:34:31.260
Go ahead, Harry.

00:34:31.335 --> 00:34:33.633
I just picked up
an unauthorized launch

00:34:33.704 --> 00:34:34.830
of the Delta Flyer.

00:34:34.906 --> 00:34:35.930
Seven's at the helm.

00:34:36.074 --> 00:34:37.268
Set a pursuit course.

00:34:37.341 --> 00:34:38.467
Acknowledged.

00:34:38.543 --> 00:34:39.737
Chakotay to the Doctor.

00:34:39.811 --> 00:34:40.937
Sick Bay here.

00:34:41.012 --> 00:34:42.206
Get down to Cargo Bay 2.

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:43.941
Run a diagnostic
on Seven's alcove.

00:34:44.015 --> 00:34:45.073
On my way.

00:34:45.149 --> 00:34:46.548
I'm glad we got that settled.

00:34:46.617 --> 00:34:47.549
Likewise.

00:34:47.618 --> 00:34:48.778
Chakotay...

00:34:48.853 --> 00:34:51.447
let's keep this one
out of our logs, huh?

00:34:51.522 --> 00:34:52.648
Gladly.

00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:12.634
She's altering course,
heading for the catapult.

00:35:12.710 --> 00:35:13.904
Maintain pursuit.

00:35:13.978 --> 00:35:15.240
Open a channel.

00:35:15.313 --> 00:35:16.678
No response.

00:35:16.747 --> 00:35:17.907
Try to beam her out.

00:35:18.015 --> 00:35:20.779
She's done something to
alter her bio-signature.

00:35:20.852 --> 00:35:21.910
I can't get a lock.

00:35:22.053 --> 00:35:24.248
Target her propulsion
and weapons.

00:35:24.322 --> 00:35:25.880
Fire.

00:35:32.330 --> 00:35:34.195
Our targeting scanners
are out of alignment.

00:35:34.265 --> 00:35:35.289
She must have done it

00:35:35.366 --> 00:35:36.492
before she took off.

00:35:36.567 --> 00:35:37.591
She's charging weapons.

00:35:37.668 --> 00:35:38.760
Keep trying.

00:35:38.836 --> 00:35:40.167
Doctor to Captain Janeway.

00:35:40.238 --> 00:35:41.830
Report.

00:35:41.906 --> 00:35:44.773
Seven downloaded too much data
into her cortical implant.

00:35:44.842 --> 00:35:45.900
She's trying to make sense

00:35:45.977 --> 00:35:47.706
of more information
than she can process.

00:35:47.778 --> 00:35:48.904
Understood.

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:51.210
Beam me onto the Delta Flyer.

00:35:51.282 --> 00:35:52.909
I'm going with you.

00:35:52.984 --> 00:35:54.952
No, I have a better chance
of getting through to her alone.

00:35:55.086 --> 00:35:57.782
This isn't part of
your mission, is it?

00:35:57.855 --> 00:35:59.379
Is it part of yours?

00:36:00.658 --> 00:36:01.886
Good luck.

00:36:01.959 --> 00:36:03.051
Energize.

00:36:09.534 --> 00:36:10.967
Captain.

00:36:13.671 --> 00:36:16.663
You came here
hoping to stop me.

00:36:16.741 --> 00:36:17.867
You'll fail.

00:36:17.942 --> 00:36:19.068
Turn this ship around.

00:36:19.143 --> 00:36:20.269
That's an order.

00:36:20.344 --> 00:36:22.403
Your orders are irrelevant.

00:36:22.480 --> 00:36:24.914
I'm no longer
under your command.

00:36:25.049 --> 00:36:26.277
You deceived me.

00:36:26.350 --> 00:36:27.874
There is no conspiracy.

00:36:27.952 --> 00:36:29.920
There is no Maquis rebellion.

00:36:30.054 --> 00:36:32.784
The Federation isn't
planning to invade

00:36:32.857 --> 00:36:34.154
the Delta Quadrant.

00:36:34.225 --> 00:36:35.556
I realize that,

00:36:35.626 --> 00:36:38.356
because I finally uncovered
your true objective.

00:36:38.429 --> 00:36:39.691
And what's that?

00:36:40.731 --> 00:36:41.993
Me.

00:36:43.501 --> 00:36:44.593
Stardate 32611.

00:36:44.669 --> 00:36:46.933
The Federation
sends my parents

00:36:47.071 --> 00:36:48.333
to study the Borg collective.

00:36:48.406 --> 00:36:50.704
They know my family
will be assimilated.

00:36:50.775 --> 00:36:52.504
That was their intention.

00:36:52.577 --> 00:36:53.737
Stardate 48317.

00:36:53.811 --> 00:36:55.540
Voyager is sent
to the Delta Quadrant

00:36:55.613 --> 00:36:56.807
with orders to retrieve me.

00:36:56.881 --> 00:36:58.439
When they reach Borg space,

00:36:58.516 --> 00:37:01.576
Captain Janeway negotiates
an alliance with the collective

00:37:01.652 --> 00:37:03.085
in exchange for information

00:37:03.154 --> 00:37:05.019
regarding Species 8472.

00:37:05.089 --> 00:37:08.252
They agree to give her
Seven of Nine.

00:37:08.326 --> 00:37:10.794
Stardate 51030.

00:37:10.861 --> 00:37:13.091
Janeway extracts
the implants from my body

00:37:13.164 --> 00:37:16.759
to remove any knowledge I have
of her agreement with the Borg.

00:37:16.834 --> 00:37:18.267
Stardate 53329.

00:37:18.336 --> 00:37:21.134
Captain Janeway finalizes plans
to use the catapult

00:37:21.205 --> 00:37:23.730
to deliver Seven of Nine
to the Alpha Quadrant,

00:37:23.808 --> 00:37:26.572
where Starfleet will dissect
and analyze the drone

00:37:26.644 --> 00:37:28.908
to gather tactical data
to fight the Borg.

00:37:29.013 --> 00:37:30.913
I won't allow you
to complete your mission.

00:37:31.015 --> 00:37:34.542
If necessary,
I'll destroy the catapult

00:37:34.619 --> 00:37:35.745
and myself.

00:37:39.023 --> 00:37:40.615
You're right, Seven.

00:37:40.691 --> 00:37:43.751
There is a conspiracy here,

00:37:43.828 --> 00:37:48.231
but I believe
it's a conspiracy of one.

00:37:48.299 --> 00:37:51.894
I've got a theory of my own.

00:37:51.969 --> 00:37:53.334
Your modified alcove

00:37:53.404 --> 00:37:56.134
threw your synaptic
patterns into chaos,

00:37:56.207 --> 00:37:58.266
and your mind
can't make sense

00:37:58.342 --> 00:38:01.505
of all the information,
so you're generating

00:38:01.579 --> 00:38:02.671
theory after theory

00:38:02.747 --> 00:38:04.874
in an attempt to bring
order to that chaos.

00:38:04.982 --> 00:38:06.108
Your reasoning is flawed.

00:38:06.183 --> 00:38:07.775
My alcove
is functioning perfectly.

00:38:07.852 --> 00:38:09.649
What about you?

00:38:09.720 --> 00:38:11.347
You're not a drone anymore.

00:38:11.422 --> 00:38:12.889
You can't always predict

00:38:12.990 --> 00:38:16.585
how Borg technology
will affect you.

00:38:16.661 --> 00:38:18.026
You should be in Sick Bay,

00:38:18.095 --> 00:38:20.188
not behind that force field.

00:38:20.264 --> 00:38:21.390
Let me help you.

00:38:21.465 --> 00:38:22.898
No.

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:24.695
I don't believe you.

00:38:24.769 --> 00:38:26.396
Of course you don't.

00:38:26.470 --> 00:38:29.906
Anything I say gets woven into
your paranoid conspiracies,

00:38:30.007 --> 00:38:31.907
but you should believe me,
Seven,

00:38:32.009 --> 00:38:34.910
because I've never lied to you.

00:38:35.012 --> 00:38:36.809
And I'm not lying to you now.

00:38:36.881 --> 00:38:40.408
You have to put
your doubts aside

00:38:40.484 --> 00:38:43.009
and trust me.

00:38:43.087 --> 00:38:47.524
Stardate 51030.

00:38:47.591 --> 00:38:50.389
Seven of Nine is severed
from the hive mind.

00:38:50.461 --> 00:38:52.929
The Captain tells
her not to resist,

00:38:53.030 --> 00:38:54.258
that she'll learn

00:38:54.332 --> 00:38:55.890
to accept her humanity.

00:38:55.966 --> 00:38:58.526
Seven complies

00:38:58.602 --> 00:39:01.662
and slowly begins
to embrace her individuality.

00:39:01.739 --> 00:39:06.267
Does she regret that decision?

00:39:06.344 --> 00:39:09.177
Stardate 51652.

00:39:09.246 --> 00:39:12.875
The Captain encourages Seven
to develop her social skills.

00:39:12.983 --> 00:39:16.248
Seven insists
it's a waste of time,

00:39:16.320 --> 00:39:18.481
but after further requests,
she pursues it

00:39:18.556 --> 00:39:22.754
and begins to develop her
first human friendships.

00:39:22.827 --> 00:39:26.263
Did Janeway lead her astray?

00:39:26.330 --> 00:39:29.891
Stardate 52840.

00:39:29.967 --> 00:39:34.529
The Captain orders Seven
to study her parents' journals.

00:39:34.605 --> 00:39:36.505
Seven claims
they're irrelevant,

00:39:36.574 --> 00:39:38.337
but eventually
she reads them

00:39:38.409 --> 00:39:40.707
and rediscovers part
of her own past.

00:39:40.778 --> 00:39:44.805
Stardate 52841.

00:39:44.882 --> 00:39:48.613
For the first time,

00:39:48.686 --> 00:39:52.816
Seven tells the Captain...
"thank you."

00:39:57.695 --> 00:40:02.359
It was Stardate 52842...

00:40:02.433 --> 00:40:06.494
0600 hours in the Mess Hall.

00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:08.629
We had just finished breakfast.

00:40:08.706 --> 00:40:11.641
My mistake.

00:40:11.709 --> 00:40:13.939
Stardate today.

00:40:14.044 --> 00:40:17.775
Janeway beams aboard
the Delta Flyer.

00:40:17.848 --> 00:40:21.579
She reminds Seven of the bond
that's grown between them.

00:40:21.652 --> 00:40:24.177
Seven lowers the force field

00:40:24.255 --> 00:40:26.951
and she decides to come home.

00:40:27.057 --> 00:40:30.652
All I'm asking

00:40:30.728 --> 00:40:33.322
is that you trust me again.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:51.944
Delta Flyer to Voyager.

00:40:52.016 --> 00:40:53.608
Two to beam out.

00:40:57.021 --> 00:40:58.613
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:40:58.689 --> 00:41:01.715
After further testing,
we activated the catapult

00:41:01.792 --> 00:41:04.556
and were hurtled across
30 sectors of space.

00:41:04.628 --> 00:41:08.223
In less than an hour, we cut
three years off our journey.

00:41:08.299 --> 00:41:09.891
I'm happy to say the Doctor

00:41:09.967 --> 00:41:12.231
has repaired Seven of Nine's
cortical processor,

00:41:12.303 --> 00:41:13.770
and she's returned to duty.

00:41:13.838 --> 00:41:15.203
Guess who assimilated

00:41:15.272 --> 00:41:17.866
three books and ten
reports in two days?

00:41:17.942 --> 00:41:19.102
Naomi Wildman.

00:41:19.176 --> 00:41:21.940
That's correct.

00:41:22.046 --> 00:41:24.276
Are you taking your
new alcove apart?

00:41:24.348 --> 00:41:25.440
Yes.

00:41:25.516 --> 00:41:26.608
Why?

00:41:26.684 --> 00:41:27.946
My attempt

00:41:28.052 --> 00:41:30.247
to download
Voyager's database failed.

00:41:30.321 --> 00:41:31.788
Maybe you can fix it.

00:41:31.856 --> 00:41:37.954
The alcove functioned
within expected parameters.

00:41:38.062 --> 00:41:39.996
Unfortunately, I did not.

00:41:42.399 --> 00:41:44.959
Three books and ten reports
is impressive,

00:41:45.069 --> 00:41:47.697
but quantity is less
relevant than quality.

00:41:47.771 --> 00:41:50.137
You must be able
to interpret the data

00:41:50.207 --> 00:41:52.232
and enjoy the process.

00:41:53.677 --> 00:41:55.804
Regardless,
you require activities

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:58.610
other than assimilating
books and reports.

00:41:58.682 --> 00:42:01.276
A game of Kadis-Kot,
for example.

00:42:01.352 --> 00:42:02.649
When?

00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:05.154
Go to the Mess Hall
and set up the board.

00:42:05.222 --> 00:42:07.156
I'll join you when I'm finished.

00:42:12.630 --> 00:42:16.930
I heard the strangest
rumor today.

00:42:17.034 --> 00:42:19.559
Apparently, the Captain
and First Officer

00:42:19.637 --> 00:42:20.934
almost came to blows.

00:42:21.038 --> 00:42:22.630
Mutiny?

00:42:22.706 --> 00:42:25.504
First Officer walked the plank.

00:42:25.576 --> 00:42:26.804
So I heard.

00:42:30.047 --> 00:42:31.639
I don't believe a word of it.

00:42:31.715 --> 00:42:33.012
Me, neither.

00:42:36.053 --> 00:42:37.953
Seven was malfunctioning.

00:42:38.055 --> 00:42:40.046
We don't have that excuse.

00:42:40.124 --> 00:42:41.751
You're right.

00:42:41.825 --> 00:42:45.693
We've been through too much
to stop trusting each other.

00:42:49.667 --> 00:42:51.532
You didn't poison
the coffee, did you?

00:42:51.602 --> 00:42:53.968
Not any more than I usually do.
